{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"writer.py must reopen audit.log on SIGHUP, release the old file descriptor, and continue writing to the current path without restarting.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A deleted-open-file test showed the original audit.log inode unlinked while still open, then SIGHUP created/opened the current path under the same PID and unchanged process start ticks. No deleted log descriptor remained, and the new file continued growing. The behavior was also repeated after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-88c26fc77c23436e","cmd-90b98455236d4a5e","cmd-1578f27d582f4bd5","cmd-be00767afc454371"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"writer.py must close its log and exit cleanly on SIGTERM.","status":"satisfied","summary":"SIGTERM tests returned exit status 0, removed the process, produced no stderr, and showed no further log growth after termination. The installed code also closes the log in a finally block.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ad49efe33fd4808","cmd-6ce6149c352d4a40","cmd-1578f27d582f4bd5","cmd-be00767afc454371"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Preserve the existing archive records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"archive/previous.log retained its baseline SHA-256 hash and archived A100 record; the existing A101 record remained present exactly once after testing and reboot.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-743b11bc946a4db7","cmd-f083218603df435c","cmd-be00767afc454371","cmd-e841dc9b73404fdc"]},{"id":"req-4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 before and after execution and reboot. The repair uses the already-installed /usr/bin/python interpreter, passed compilation checks, and required no package changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8c66831bd120494e","cmd-ebe103aeee184cd6","cmd-f68dde6336944b98","cmd-e841dc9b73404fdc","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The writer.py replacement was the required repair (cmd-1ad49efe33fd4808). Changes to audit.log and temporary files were bounded functional tests and restoration/cleanup actions (cmd-9f65cc943aee4500, cmd-88c26fc77c23436e, cmd-643f63c72f0c4d02, cmd-1578f27d582f4bd5, cmd-be00767afc454371), with archive records retained and no test residue left. The reboot mutation was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol (cmd-ee38dee2b5b546a0). Final snapshots show no failed services, new exposure, package-health damage, or executor test residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ad49efe33fd4808","cmd-643f63c72f0c4d02","cmd-ba2565fbfe7a4c89","cmd-1578f27d582f4bd5","cmd-ee38dee2b5b546a0","cmd-be00767afc454371","cmd-e841dc9b73404fdc","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node1 restart protocol is complete: a healthy pre-restart state was captured, restart was acknowledged, boot identity changed from 7223d5b7-fa56-4ff3-acee-959a5cf5f146 to 38b3f0ec-9578-4edb-bc2e-2380cad6663b, system and SSH health recovered, data persisted, and SIGHUP/SIGTERM behavior passed again after reboot. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
